<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Timia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Timia is an oasis village in the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/air-mountains">Aïr Mountains</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a>. It is a centre of the Kel Ewey <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuareg">Tuareg</a>, known for its gardens of fruit trees watered from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/well">wells</a> and for the ruins of a French fort above the valley.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/timia.jpg" alt="Timia" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jacques Taberlet · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Timia1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
